// THE REFUSE HALF OF THE MEET AT THE CALL (PROBES.md 2026-08-31n), one field
// from tests/logos/pass/bc_ltcallmeet_callee_binder_meet: `t` holds its
// `&'tcx i64` BEHIND a `&mut`, so 'tcx occurs under MutRef's POINTEE and the
// variance fixpoint reads `FnCtxt.@1 = Inv` (measured directly, LOGOS_CENSUS
// `var.…@1=Inv`). An invariant occurrence demands EQUALITY of the two offered
// regions and no meet discharges that, so the binder keeps first-occurrence-
// wins and the second argument is refused.
//
// ⚠ THIS FILE IS THE ONLY THING IN THE TREE THAT SEPARATES THE GUARD FROM ITS
// ABSENCE. `ltcallmeetany` — the same site with the covariance guard removed —
// prices IDENTICALLY to the guarded arm on all three populations (ceiling 23,
// cost 3, the same rows, the same 1056-row fail table). It compiles this
// program. If a later round widens the guard, this fixture is what goes green.
//
// ⚠ `&'tcx mut i64` IS NOT THE INVARIANT SPELLING: the REGION of a `&mut` is
// itself covariant and only its POINTEE is invariant. That spelling is
// admitted, measured, and it is why this one is written with the nesting.
package bc_ltcallmeet_invariant_binder_no_meet;

struct FnCtxt<'a, 'tcx> { a: &'a i64, t: &'a mut &'tcx i64 }

fn use_it<'a, 'tcx>(f: &FnCtxt<'a, 'tcx>, x: &'tcx i64) {}

fn use_fcx<'a, 'tcx>(f: &FnCtxt<'a, 'tcx>) -> &'a i64 { return f.a; }

fn bad_method<'a, 'tcx>(fcx: &FnCtxt<'a, 'tcx>) {
    let other = use_fcx(fcx);
    use_it(fcx, other);
}

fn main() -> i32 { return 0i32; }
